## 4) Exact screenshot-bytes validation (`normalizeScreenshotBytes`, lines 16–35)

Command: `rg -n '' scripts/line_backup_cua_adapter.mjs | sed -n '16,35p'`

```
16:export function normalizeScreenshotBytes(value) {
17:  requireFact(ArrayBuffer.isView(value), 'CAPTURE_BYTES_INVALID');
18:  let tag, buffer, byteOffset, byteLength, backingLength;
19:  try {
20:    tag = Reflect.apply(typedArrayTag, value, []);
21:    buffer = Reflect.apply(typedArrayBuffer, value, []);
22:    byteOffset = Reflect.apply(typedArrayByteOffset, value, []);
23:    byteLength = Reflect.apply(typedArrayByteLength, value, []);
24:    backingLength = Reflect.apply(arrayBufferByteLength, buffer, []);
25:  } catch {
26:    throw new Error('CAPTURE_BYTES_INVALID');
27:  }
28:  requireFact(tag === 'Uint8Array' && Number.isSafeInteger(byteOffset) && byteOffset >= 0
29:    && Number.isSafeInteger(byteLength) && byteLength > 0 && byteLength <= 16 * 1024 * 1024
30:    && Number.isSafeInteger(backingLength) && byteOffset + byteLength <= backingLength,
31:  'CAPTURE_BYTES_INVALID');
32:  const copy = new Uint8Array(byteLength);
33:  copy.set(new Uint8Array(buffer, byteOffset, byteLength));
34:  return copy;
35:}
```

Rejection conditions, all error code `CAPTURE_BYTES_INVALID` (via `requireFact`, line 5: `const requireFact = (ok, code) => {if (!ok) throw new Error(code);};`):
- Line 17: `!ArrayBuffer.isView(value)` → throw.
- Lines 19–26: any of the 5 intrinsic getters throwing when invoked via `Reflect.apply` → `throw new Error('CAPTURE_BYTES_INVALID')`.
- Lines 28–31 (all must hold simultaneously or throw): intrinsic getter tag `=== 'Uint8Array'`; `Number.isSafeInteger(byteOffset) && byteOffset >= 0`; `Number.isSafeInteger(byteLength) && byteLength > 0 && byteLength <= 16 * 1024 * 1024` (16 MiB = 16777216); `Number.isSafeInteger(backingLength) && byteOffset + byteLength <= backingLength`.
- On success: byte-for-byte copy into a fresh `Uint8Array(byteLength)` (32–33) — so foreign-realm views and `Buffer.subarray` offset views are normalized (confirmed by tests at tests/test_cua_adapter.mjs:53–70).
- The getters used come from module-level intrinsics at lines 9–14: `typedArrayTag`/`typedArrayBuffer`/`typedArrayByteOffset`/`typedArrayByteLength` from `Object.getPrototypeOf(Uint8Array.prototype)`, and `arrayBufferByteLength` from `ArrayBuffer.prototype`.

