```
(Note: navigation's version has no `closed` operand; hosted's has `!stopped`.)

When it happens relative to retain/classify: `fresh()` is *not* called inside `observe()`. It is called at each act site, after the capture was retained and classified, using the timestamp captured *before* `getAXStateAndScreenshot` (`requestStartedAtMonotonic` at 110 stored as `latest.at` at 130; navigation `started` at 504 stored as `latest.started` at 519). Comment at line 129: `// The capture interval starts before CUA and never renews during persistence/OCR.` So retain/classify time consumes the 5000 ms window rather than resetting it. Each GUI input path also clears `latest = null` before acting (e.g. `reserveGui` line 100, `openAlbum` line 151, `calibrateMenu` lines 168/185, `originalAtomicDispatch` line 246, `exactChooser` line 309), so a previously classified frame cannot be reused after a new action begins.

Related but separate 5000 ms use (line 227, `originalIntent` permit): `deadline:latest.at+5000` — the one-shot dispatch permit's deadline is the capture-start timestamp + 5000 ms.

Representative act-side `fresh(...)` call sites: 148, 158, 214, 219, 240, 299, 317, 391, 468, 527, 538.

